Based on the provided context, here are the step-by-step instructions to deploy a containerized application on AWS using ECS:

**Step 1: Create an IAM Role for Your Container Instances**

* Go to the IAM console at [https://console.aws.amazon.com/iam/](https://console.aws.amazon.com/iam/)
* In the navigation pane, choose **Roles** and select the IAM role to use for your container instances. This role is likely titled `ecsInstanceRole`. For more information, see [Amazon ECS container instance IAM role](instance_IAM_role.md) [Source: aws/ECS/What is Amazon Elastic Container Service?<a name="Welcome"></a>]

**Step 2: Create an ECS Cluster**

* Use the AWS CDK to define a containerized web server on Fargate. Update `src/main/java/com.myorg/HelloEcsStack.java` so that it resembles the following:
```java
import software.amazon.awscdk.services.ecs.Cluster;

public class HelloEcsStack extends Stack {
    public HelloEcsStack(Construct scope, String id) {
        super(scope, id);

        Cluster cluster = new Cluster(this, "MyWebServer");

        // Define your containerized web server on Fargate
        ContainerDefinition container = new ContainerDefinition(this, "MyWebServerContainer")
            .setImage("amazon/amazon-ecs-sample")
            .setPortMappings(new PortMapping(80));

        // Add the container to the cluster
        cluster.addContainer(container);
    }
}
```
[Source: aws/ECS/Getting started with Amazon ECS using the AWS CDK<a name="tutorial-ecs-web-server-cdk"></a> > Step 2: Use the AWS CDK to define a containerized web server on Fargate<a name="ecs-web-server-cdk-step-2"></a>]

**Step 3: Configure Your Container Instance**

* Update `src/HelloEcs/HelloEcsStack.cs` so that it resembles the following:
```csharp
using Amazon.ECS;
using Amazon.ECS.Model;

public class HelloEcsStack : Stack
{
    public HelloEcsStack(Construct scope, string id)
    {
        base(scope, id);

        // Define your containerized web server on Fargate
        ContainerDefinition container = new ContainerDefinition(this, "MyWebServerContainer")
            .setImage("amazon/amazon-ecs-sample")
            .setPortMappings(new PortMapping(80));

        // Add the container to the cluster
        Cluster cluster = new Cluster(this, "MyWebServer");
        cluster.AddContainer(container);
    }
}
```
[Source: aws/ECS/Getting started with Amazon ECS using the AWS CDK<a name="tutorial-ecs-web-server-cdk"></a> > Step 2: Use the AWS CDK to define a containerized web server on Fargate<a name="ecs-web-server-cdk-step-2"></a>]

**Step 4: Deploy Your Application**

* Run the `cdk synth` command in your application's main directory. The AWS CDK will create all the resources that are required to deploy the web server, including the ECS cluster, VPC, EC2 instances, Auto Scaling group, Application Load Balancer, and IAM roles and policies.
* Run the `cdk deploy` command in your application's main directory. You're asked to approve the IAM policies that the AWS CDK generated.

Note: These instructions are based on the provided context and may not be a comprehensive guide for deploying a containerized application on AWS using ECS.
